content.text:
Found the bug. The root cause is on line 83:

```css
html, body {
  height: 100%;
  ...
}
```

Combined with `body { overflow-y: auto }`, this makes the `body` a **nested scroll container** exactly 100vh tall. The browser's window-level scroll (tied to the `html` element) sees nothing to scroll because `html` is also capped at 100%, so you get stuck. The fix: change `height: 100%` to `min-height: 100%` on both — they stay at least full-viewport tall but can grow taller, letting the window scroll work normally. The research view (`overflow: hidden` + `app { height: 100vh }`) still works because the `.app` fills the viewport and body scroll is locked.

